-- title:
--   Conjugating a maximal quaternion order by a finite idele
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the quaternion algebra $H=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is a maximal order in the sense of the project's predicate [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsMaximalOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_EichlerOrder.html#L63): $\Lambda$ is an order, i.e. $1\in\Lambda$, $\Lambda$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of $\Lambda$ is all of $H$ and $\Lambda$ is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$; and moreover every $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $\Lambda'$ of $H$ that is an order in this same sense and contains $\Lambda$ is equal to $\Lambda$. Let $\beta$ be a unit of $H\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$, where $\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ is the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$. The conclusion is that [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele Λ β`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31) is again a maximal order in the same sense, where this submodule is defined as the preimage, under $z\mapsto z\otimes 1$ from $H$ into $H\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$, of the image of $\widehat{\Lambda}$ under $x\mapsto\beta x\beta^{-1}$; here $\widehat{\Lambda}$ is the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele integral at every height-one prime of $\mathbb{Z}$.
--
--   This is the statement that $H\cap\beta\widehat{\Lambda}\beta^{-1}$ is a maximal order whenever $\Lambda$ is, the basic stability property underlying the adelic description of the set of maximal (and, after intersecting, Eichler) orders in a quaternion algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld tower constructions, where Hecke-type elements of the finite idele group act on orders of a given level.
-- source:
